&lt;h2&gt;What is Claude AI for marketing?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude AI for marketing means using Claude, Anthropic’s AI assistant, to handle the writing, research, and analysis work that campaigns depend on. Claude helps marketers draft, analyze, and summarize work, such as writing and editing first drafts, turning meeting notes into briefs, and assembling campaign readouts from numbers in separate analytics tools. It can also pull current information from the web, which makes it handy for early-stage market research.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;As with all large language models (LLMs), the quality of Claude’s output depends heavily on the context it receives. &lt;a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/claude-prompting-best-practices"&gt;Anthropic’s prompting guidance&lt;/a&gt; compares Claude to a sharp new employee with no background on how your team operates, and it recommends telling Claude who the output is for and how it will be used.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude works well on its own for one-off drafting and research. It becomes far more powerful once it can read your real customer records, campaign results, and engagement history.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why connect Claude to HubSpot?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Picture a marketer asking Claude why last quarter’s webinar series underperformed. Without a link to HubSpot, Claude can only work with what gets pasted into the chat: an exported spreadsheet, a few copied metrics, a paragraph describing the audience. Each fresh analysis means exporting and explaining that background again, and the answer stops wherever the export does.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Connected workflows move that context gathering out of the marketer’s hands. The HubSpot connector for Claude links HubSpot context to Claude, giving it read access to contacts, deals, campaigns, marketing emails, and other records, scoped to each person’s current HubSpot access rights. Logged calls, meetings, emails, tasks, and notes are readable too, unless the account has Sensitive Data turned on. The webinar question can now pull event records, follow-up activity, and campaign attribution data into a single answer.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The connection also runs in reverse. Claude can create and update HubSpot records, such as changing a deal stage or adding a task, from the chat window, though it can’t delete data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot Smart CRM unifies customer context and campaign records. It sits beneath Marketing Hub, Sales Hub, and HubSpot’s other core products as their shared database, showing where each contact stands at every point in the relationship. Claude then works from one consistent record rather than fragments stitched together from separate tools. Connected AI workflows improve &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-personalization-growth"&gt;personalization&lt;/a&gt; and execution for that reason.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Getting there takes a one-time setup in Claude’s connector settings.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How to Connect Claude to HubSpot Using the HubSpot Connector for Claude&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/test-2-20261030-4085970.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Claude AI for marketing connectors list showing HubSpot integration with connect button"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/claude"&gt;HubSpot connector for Claude&lt;/a&gt; is free, but it requires a paid Claude plan (Pro, Max, Team, or Enterprise) and an active HubSpot user account on any plan, including free. Super Admins and users with App Marketplace Access permissions can connect immediately; everyone else needs Super Admin approval first.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Then, in Claude:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ol start="3"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Log in to the HubSpot account you want to use.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Select the permissions to grant, then click &lt;strong&gt;Connect app&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ol&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;What the Connector Does&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/test-4-20261030-2782831.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Claude AI for marketing welcome screen displaying daily pipeline pulse with HubSpot deals"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Toggling HubSpot on under &lt;strong&gt;+&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Connectors&lt;/strong&gt; in any chat lets Claude reference your HubSpot records in its answers. Set the connector’s &lt;em&gt;Write tools&lt;/em&gt; option to &lt;em&gt;Needs Approval&lt;/em&g...

&lt;p&gt;As you scroll through your TikTok or Instagram feed, you’ll no doubt come across at least a handful of influencers trying to sell you something by wearing the latest viral lip gloss, hopping into luxury cars, and taste-testing popular treats. But what if I told you that while these content creators may look like real people, they’re actually AI influencers?&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you’re a marketer or business owner who is already fully using AI in your digital marketing strategy, then you’re likely already familiar with the concept. You may even be curious about leveraging AI influencers in your influencer marketing strategy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=b0f73a5e-16e4-41fd-9511-8564efc560a7&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: Free State of Marketing Report [Updated for 2026]" height="79" width="423" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/b0f73a5e-16e4-41fd-9511-8564efc560a7.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But how will your target consumers feel about the use of AI influencers? Will they be receptive, or can AI influencers erode the trust you’ve built with your audience? Can AI influencers really save you money compared to working with human influencers? And are all virtual influencers AI? Keep reading for answers to these questions and more.&lt;/p&gt; 
